    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d656">

                <pb facs="0541" n="459" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg459"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Governor of Arizona to
                        the President.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Douglas, Ariz.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-04-17"><hi rendition="#italic">April 17,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>As a result of to-day’s fighting across the international line, but within
                    gunshot range of the heartof Douglas, five Americans wounded on this side of the
                    line. Everything points to repetition of these casualties on to-morrow, and
                    while the Federals seem disposed to keep their agreement not to fire into
                    Douglas, the position of the insurrectionists is such that when fighting occurs
                    on the east and southeast of the intrenchments people living in Douglas are put
                    in danger of their lives. In my judgment radical measures are needed to protect
                    our innocent people, and if anything can be done to stop the fighting at Agua
                    Prieta the situation calls for such action. It is impossible to safeguard the
                    people of Douglas unless the town be vacated. Can anything be done to relieve
                    situation, now acute?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard E. Sloan</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Governor.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
